	<text xml:lang="la">
		<note xml:id="fn1" type="footnote" subtype="metadata" n="1">Wann <persName ref="p1283" cert="high">Geßner</persName> <placeName ref="l59" cert="high">Bourges</placeName> verließ und nach <placeName ref="l378" cert="high">Paris</placeName> ging, läßt sich nicht nachweisen. Denkbar wäre ein Zeitpunkt im Frühsommer 1534, wird er doch Mitte Mai von <persName ref="p495" cert="high">Bullinger</persName> noch in <placeName ref="l59" cert="high">Bourges</placeName> vermutet (s. oben S. 174, 36f).</note>
		<body>
			<div xml:id="div1" corresp="regest1">
				<p>
					<s n="1" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z1"/>S.</s>
					<s n="2" xml:lang="la">Iam fere annus est, qui nobis tamen vel seculum videtur, quod nihil <lb xml:id="p1z2"/>a vobis literarum accepimus<note xml:id="fn2" type="footnote" n="2">Demnach ist anzunehmen, daß <persName ref="p1283">Geßner</persName> und <persName ref="p1214">Fries</persName> <persName ref="p495">Bullingers</persName> Brief vom 12. Mai 1534 (oben <ref target="file10407">Nr. 374</ref>) nicht erhalten haben, obschon dieser sowohl nach <placeName ref="l378">Paris</placeName> als auch nach <placeName ref="l59">Bourges</placeName> adressiert war (s. oben S. 174, 36f).</note>.</s>
					<s n="3" xml:lang="la">Alii diuturno silentio sepe in alienam <lb xml:id="p1z3"/>atque secus, quam res habeat, opinionem veniunt.</s>
					<s n="4" xml:lang="la">Sed vestra in nos <lb xml:id="p1z4"/>propensa voluntas atque studium etiam sine literis et, ut ita <lb xml:id="p1z5"/>dicam, sine tessera nunquam non testatissima nobis erunt.</s>
					<s n="5" xml:lang="la">Sollicite <lb xml:id="p1z6"/>tamen interim et quasi aperto sinu puerorum instar literas <lb xml:id="p1z7"/>a vobis et avide expectamus et tacite poscimus, quo cum <lb xml:id="p1z8"/>de nostratibus omnibus, tum vero de te pręcipue et patria certi<lb xml:id="p1z9"/>ores fiamus: <foreign xml:lang="el">ὡς οὐδὲν γλύκιον ἧς πατρίδος</foreign> - nosti <persName ref="p18514">Homerica</persName><note xml:id="fn3" type="footnote" n="3"><persName ref="p18514">Homer</persName>, Odyssee IX, 34.</note>.<pb type="edition" next="291"/></s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="6" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z10"/>Quod ad nos, <persName ref="p167">Ammiano</persName> scripsimus<note xml:id="fn4" type="footnote" n="4">Ein Brief von <persName ref="p1283">Geßner</persName> oder <persName ref="p1214">Johannes Fries</persName> an <persName ref="p167">Johann Jakob Ammann</persName> ist nicht erhalten.</note>, quem si modo redditae sunt, <lb xml:id="p1z11"/>rem omnem tibi aperuisse arbitror.</s>
					<s n="7" xml:lang="la">Te cuius es humanitatis <lb xml:id="p1z12"/>clientes non neglecturum speramus atque adeo certi de fide <lb xml:id="p1z13"/>tua sumus.</s>
					<s n="8" xml:lang="la">Spes fere dubia esse solet, <foreign xml:lang="el">ό δὲ ἀνέλπιστος βίος <lb xml:id="p1z14"/>ἄριστος</foreign>.</s>
					<s n="9" xml:lang="la">Nos quoque iam olim multis, iisque magnis, tibi nomini<lb xml:id="p1z15"/>bus obligati certam magis tuam benignitatem fidemque quam <lb xml:id="p1z16"/>spe conceptam habemus.</s>
					<s n="10" xml:lang="la">Amaltheam inter sidera collocatam <lb xml:id="p1z17"/>ferunt, quae lovem nutrisset.</s>
					<s n="11" xml:lang="la">Tu vero quantam laudem <lb xml:id="p1z18"/>merebere musas love prognatas tam candide tam liberaliter <lb xml:id="p1z19"/>fovendo!</s>
					<s n="12" xml:lang="la">Non alia musis <foreign xml:lang="el">θρεπτήρια</foreign> reddes, nisi quę <lb xml:id="p1z20"/>in earum studiosos contuleris.</s>
					<s n="13" xml:lang="la">Verum hęc hactenus.</s>
					<s n="14" xml:lang="la">Pecuniam quam <lb xml:id="p1z21"/>maturrime mitti vellemus.</s>
					<s n="15" xml:lang="la">Nosti illud <foreign xml:lang="el">ἡ πενία χωλὸς πρὸς <lb xml:id="p1z22"/>τὸ φιλοσοφεῖν</foreign>, quamvis <foreign xml:lang="el">πενίαν</foreign> <persName ref="p18457">Diogenes</persName> <foreign xml:lang="el">φιλοσοφία<lb xml:id="p1z23"/>ν αὐτοδίδακτον</foreign> vocarit<note xml:id="fn5" type="footnote" n="5"><persName ref="p17877">Dionysius von Halikarnass</persName>, Antiqu. rom. 5, 12.</note>.</s>
					<s n="16" xml:lang="la">Pergimus in literis pro virili perrecturi <lb xml:id="p1z24"/>amplius, nisi hic etiam ipsę musę pecunia flectendę essent ut <lb xml:id="p1z25"/>aureo malo <persName ref="p20096">Hippodameia</persName><note xml:id="fn6" type="footnote" ana="bio" n="6"><persName ref="p20096">Hippodamea</persName>, Tochter des <persName ref="p20995">Önomaus</persName>, die, <persName ref="p20996">Pelops</persName> dank einem durch Bestechung gewonnenen Wagenrennen zur Gattin erhielt (<bibl source="b247">Georges</bibl> I 3056f).</note>.</s>
					<s n="17" xml:lang="la">Verum et hic et in aliis omnibus argent<lb xml:id="p1z26"/>i <persName ref="p19902">Charybdin</persName><note xml:id="fn7" type="footnote" n="7"><persName ref="p19902">Charybdis</persName> als Inbegriff der Habgier, vgl. <bibl source="b56">Adagia</bibl>, 3, 7, 41 (<bibl source="b370">LB</bibl> II 892f).</note> <placeName ref="l378">Parisios</placeName> dixeris.</s>
					<s n="18" xml:lang="la">Nos interim, quod eius licet, <lb xml:id="p1z27"/>frugaliter et parce, neque id sine musis, aetatem agimus.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="19" xml:lang="la" ana="farewell"><lb xml:id="p1z28"/>Vale, praesidium et dulce decus<note xml:id="fn8" type="footnote" n="8"><persName ref="p19882">Horaz</persName>, carm. 1, 1, 2.</note> nostrum.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="20" xml:lang="la"><placeName ref="l378">Parisiis</placeName>, 7. calendas septembris <lb xml:id="p1z29"/>1534.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<s n="21" xml:lang="la"><lb xml:id="p1z30"/><persName ref="p1283">Conradus Gessnerus</persName>, ex <lb xml:id="p1z31"/>animo tuus.</s>
				</p>
				<p>
					<note type="address">[Adresse auf der Rückseite:]</note>
					<s n="22" xml:lang="la"><pb/><lb xml:id="p2z1"/>Eximio viro d. <persName ref="p495">Henrico <lb xml:id="p2z2"/>Bullingero</persName> <placeName ref="l587">Tiguri</placeName> a sacris concionibus, <lb xml:id="p2z3"/>patrono studiorum <lb xml:id="p2z4"/>optimo.</s>
					<s n="23" xml:lang="de"><lb xml:id="p2z5"/><placeName ref="l587">Zürich</placeName>.</s>
				</p>
			</div>
		</body>
	</text>
